{{!--
    The Director's log: one field, always on.

    Running the session and recording it are ONE act (doctrine Law 15), so this
    is a single text input and nothing else — no dialog, no form, no save
    button. The GM types the meaning; the console attaches the timestamp,
    scene, mode and current subject.

    A leading recognised word plus a colon ("npc: the caretaker lies") becomes
    a tag. That is an accelerator, never a requirement — see core/log-entry.mjs.

    The last few entries are shown as a receipt: without one, a GM has no way
    to tell a saved note from a swallowed one.
--}}
<div class="bi-log">
    {{!-- name= is load-bearing, not decoration: ApplicationV2 only restores
         focus across a part re-render when the focused element has an id or a
         name (handlebars-application.mjs _preSyncPartState). Without it the
         GM loses the caret every time a log entry lands. --}}
    <input type="text" name="bi-log-entry" class="bi-log__input" data-bi-log-input
        placeholder="{{localize 'BLANKINHERITANCE.Console.Log.Placeholder'}}"
        aria-label="{{localize 'BLANKINHERITANCE.Console.Log.Placeholder'}}" autocomplete="off">
    <ul class="bi-log__recent">
        {{#each entries}}
        <li class="bi-log__entry">
            {{#if this.tag}}<span class="bi-log__tag">{{this.tag}}</span>{{/if}}
            <span class="bi-log__text">{{this.text}}</span>
        </li>
        {{else}}
        <li class="bi-log__entry bi-log__entry--empty">{{localize "BLANKINHERITANCE.Console.Log.Empty"}}</li>
        {{/each}}
    </ul>
</div>
